{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>The land which we passed through to spy out.</b> To spy out the place and its inhabitants, as it says: וּרְאִיתֶם אֶת הָאָרֶץ מַה הִיא וְאֶת הָעָם הַיֹּשֵׁב עָלֶיהָ (Numbers 13:18)." "<b>The land is good.</b> Regarding what the land itself is, we testify that it is a very, very good place without blemish — not as our companions testified, saying that although it flows with milk and honey, it devours its inhabitants. And regarding the people dwelling on it, we testify that they are our bread, and they will not show a bold face against us — the opposite of our companions' testimony when they said כִּי עַז הָעָם."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:39:43.979914269Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}